// Island Birth: phase changes that build land.
//
// Dusk on a basalt sea coast. A lava lake brims on the cliff top behind a
// cornice that overhangs the sea, and drains through three vents in the
// cornice floor at the orifice (Torricelli) rate: three glowing curtains fall
// ten metres straight into the sea. Where they hit, water touching lava
// flashes to steam and obsidian; the obsidian skin crumbles to gravel, and
// lava freezing in the water or on rubble becomes rubble, so a dark cone of
// new rock grows up from the seabed. By 12 s it breaks the surface and the
// falls land on their own island: a glowing lava dome, steaming where its
// flanks meet the sea, with a strait of water between it and the cliff.
// From 14 s the eruption wanes (the lake level drops and the curtains thin),
// at 18 s the vents crust shut and the curtains' tails fall away, and the
// lake and the island cool through orange and red until they freeze into
// basalt: a new black island in the sea.
//
// Scripted parts. The lake is refilled each tick (the supply), the cooling is
// a temperature ramp over the lake and the island (radiative cooling, which
// the engine does not model, would take minutes), steam aloft is held above
// its condensing point so the plume rises instead of raining back as streaks,
// and steam and hot air that collect under the overhang are vented.
[scene]
name = island birth
description = Three lava curtains pour from a cliff-top lava lake into the sea, steam boils off the entry, a cone of new rock grows up from the seabed until it breaks the surface as a glowing island, then the vents crust shut and the island cools into black basalt.
bounds = 0 -200 640 360
seed = 0x15b1
wind = 4
ticks = 1680

[build]
fill 0 -90 640 -80 bedrock
fill 0 354 640 360 bedrock
fill 190 245 640 354 water
terrain 190 640 318 8 40 sand 354
terrain 200 400 302 4 20 sand 354
fill 0 142 200 354 bedrock
